@startuml document_processing_sequence
skinparam shadowing false

title Processing sequence — PDDL engine

actor User
participant "Frontend\n(Web/Telegram/CLI, via REST API)" as Front
participant "PddlAccessibilityOrchestrator\nbackend/agents/pddl_orchestrator.py" as Orchestrator
participant "ToolboxManifestExtractor\nbackend/core/manifest" as Manifest
participant "PlannerAgent\nbackend/core/planning" as Planner
participant "ExecutorAgent\n(Agno Workflow)" as Executor
participant "VisionAgent / DataAgent\n(Agno LLM)" as Agents
participant "Acessilia Toolbox\n(via acessilia-sdk)" as Toolbox
participant "Canonical builder\nbackend/pipeline" as Builder
participant "Renderers\nbackend/export" as Export

User -> Front: Upload a document (PDF/image)
Front -> Orchestrator: executar(file_path)

Orchestrator -> Manifest: extract(document)
Manifest -> Toolbox: structure extraction (regions, tables, OCR)
Toolbox --> Manifest: structure
Manifest --> Orchestrator: processing manifest (elements + obligations)

Orchestrator -> Planner: plan(manifest)
Planner --> Orchestrator: validated PDDL plan

Orchestrator -> Executor: run(plan, manifest)
loop each plan step
  alt deterministic method
    Executor -> Executor: docstruct algorithm
  else Toolbox method
    Executor -> Toolbox: capability (pdf.render, math.recognize, ...)
    Toolbox --> Executor: result
  else AI method
    Executor -> Agents: describe image / structure table or formula
    Agents --> Executor: typed output
  end
end
Executor --> Orchestrator: execution report

note over Orchestrator, Toolbox
  A Toolbox failure is retried or fails over, then fails
  the job with an explicit error: there is no local fallback.
end note

Orchestrator -> Builder: build_canonical_document()
note over Orchestrator, Builder
  List items retain their structure inside callouts.
  TXT keeps numeric inline values as signed digits.
end note
Builder --> Orchestrator: validated canonical document

Orchestrator -> Export: render formats
Export -> Toolbox: PDF/UA render
Export --> Front: accessible files (TXT, DOCX, PDF, PDF/UA, HTML, MP3)
Front --> User: deliver the accessible document

@enduml
